      "worked": "The doubled rectangle is similar to the original after rotation, so corresponding side ratios are equal.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x}{1}&=\\frac2x\\\\x^2&=2\\\\x&=\\pm\\sqrt2\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $x$ is a length, $x=\\sqrt2$.",
